JCAN(1)                        ZOAU Command Syntax                       JCAN(1)

NAME

	jcan - Use an operator command to cancel a job, purge a job, or both.

SYNOPSIS

	jcan [-dhv] <ACTION> <JOBNAME> <JOBNUM>

	-d
		Print out debug messages.

	-h
		Display syntax help.

	-v
		Print out verbose command information.

DESCRIPTION

	Use an operator command to cancel a job, purge a job, or both.

	ACTION must be 'C' (cancel) or 'P' (purge).

	JOBNAME can be a job name or job name pattern.

	JOBNUM can be a job number in format 'JOBnnnn' or '//' for all jobs.

	If the 'P' action is used on a job, it will be both canceled and purged.
	If the job is not in a state where it can be canceled, it will just be
	purged.

AUTHORIZATION

	The jcan utility requires authorization to use. The submitting user
	must have READ access to the MVS.MCSOPER.ZOAU profile in the OPERCMD
	class. Uisng jcan without this authority results in an error message.

	To cancel a job submitted by another user, the JESJOBS class
	must be active with generics enabled, and the submitting user must have
	ALTER authority to the resource CANCEL.nodename.user.jobname in the
	JESJOBS class.

	For example, to grant the user USERB the authority to cancel jobs
	submitted by the user USERA with a job name of JOBNAME, enter the
	following TSO commands in the order listed:

		tsocmd "SETROPTS GENERIC(JESJOBS)"
		tsocmd "RDEFINE JESJOBS CANCEL.*.USERA.JOBNAME UACC(NONE)"
		tsocmd "PERMIT CANCEL.*.USERA.JOBNAME CLASS(JESJOBS) ID(USERB)
				ACCESS(ALTER)"
		tsocmd "SETROPTS RACLIST(JESJOBS) REFRESH"

	To verify that the JESJOBS class is active, use the following TSO command:

		tsocmd "SETROPTS LIST"

	If the JESJOBS class is not active, you can activate it by entering the
	following TSO commands in the order listed:

		tsocmd "SETROPTS GENERIC(JESJOBS)"
		tsocmd "SETROPTS CLASSACT(JESJOBS)"
		tsocmd "SETROPTS RACLIST(JESJOBS)"
		tsocmd "SETROPTS RACLIST(JESJOBS) REFRESH"
		tsocmd "SETROPTS RACLIST(JESJOBS)"

ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES

	The following environment variables can be used to alter the behavior of
	`jcan`.

	CONCHAR
		Set the JES command prefix character to be used in the cancel command.
		The default prefix character for JES2 is '$', and for JES3 it is '*'.

		Set this if your installation uses a non-default command prefix
		character, or if you have multiple JES-es running simultaneously.

		For more information about JES command prefix characters, see the
		z/OS documentation:

		https://www.ibm.com/docs/en/zos/latest?topic=set-specifying-jes2-command-message-prefixes

EXAMPLES

	Cancels JOB0001 with jobname IBMUSERX:

		jcan C IBMUSERX JOB0001

	Cancels and purges all jobs with jobname IBMUSERX:

		jcan P IBMUSERX //

EXIT VALUES

	0
		Success

	Other
		Error, see message for details

